# Verification resources

Keep actual TLA+/Alloy models and configurations in models/ when required.
Keep correctness arguments and machine proof sources in proofs/ when required.
For each task name the commitment, property, abstraction, assumptions, command/tool version,
input bounds, applicable positive/negative controls and result location.
Report unexecuted, failed and bounded passing results separately. A model check is not a code proof.
Do not generate placeholder models, tautological assertions or a permanent passing-result field.
